WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.600
Now a killer you can’t see or smell.

2
00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:04.725
Carbon monoxide.

3
00:00:04.975 --> 00:00:11.125
It’s colorless, odorless, and deadly, and it’s in the exhaust of every engine and generator.

4
00:00:11.375 --> 00:00:17.200
It collects near the stern, on and around the swim platform, and in enclosed cabins.

5
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.425
It can follow you, too.

6
00:00:19.675 --> 00:00:26.050
Underway, the airflow behind the boat can pull exhaust back aboard, especially with canvas up.

7
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.975
That’s called the station wagon effect.

8
00:00:29.225 --> 00:00:33.050
The early symptoms are headache, nausea and dizziness.

9
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.600
What does that sound like on a boat?

10
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.250
Seasickness.

11
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:44.225
So when a passenger feels sick in the cabin with the generator running, don’t assume it’s the waves.

12
00:00:44.475 --> 00:00:46.500
Get them into fresh air.

13
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:51.325
Install and test carbon monoxide alarms in enclosed spaces.

14
00:00:51.575 --> 00:00:56.675
And nobody hangs on the swim platform with an engine or generator running.

15
00:00:56.925 --> 00:00:58.275
Ever.
